ent_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Fri","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":147.0689732078124,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":47.621564,"r":56.95886197552836,"t":162.6926960078124},"charspan":[0,3],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/37","text":"Fri"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Sat","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":105.43597760781245,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":47.621564,"r":56.95886197552836,"t":124.2362612078125},"charspan":[0,3],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/38","text":"Sat"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Sun","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":72.6438705078125,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":47.68066099999999,"r":57.01795897552835,"t":92.79885810781252},"charspan":[0,3],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/39","text":"Sun"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"TRAINING ZONES","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":729.9081913078126,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":310.5070978,"r":443.1950978000001,"t":743.1044413078125},"charspan":[0,14],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/40","text":"TRAINING ZONES"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"USING THESE T raining Zones will help you train at the right intensity for each session. This helps develop specific aspects of your fitness, as well as making sure you don't overdo it.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":700.1876169187746,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":310.62989999999996,"r":540.8948999999997,"t":721.2754536078124},"charspan":[0,185],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/41","text":"USING THESE T raining Zones will help you train at the right intensity for each session. This helps develop specific aspects of your fitness, as well as making sure you don't overdo it."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"You can either estimate your intensity using the Training Zone descriptions, or use a heart-rate monitor for a more precise measure. If you use a heart-rate monitor, use the percentages provided and subtract them from your maximum heart rate to calculate your zones. Tools like cycle power meters and GPS watches will also help track your training progress, but they're not essential for these plans.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":649.5356169187747,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":310.62989999999996,"r":545.1508999999988,"t":693.1144536078125},"charspan":[0,400],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/42","text":"You can either estimate your intensity using the Training Zone descriptions, or use a heart-rate monitor for a more precise measure. If you use a heart-rate monitor, use the percentages provided and subtract them from your maximum heart rate to calculate your zones. Tools like cycle power meters and GPS watches will also help track your training progress, but they're not essential for these plans."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"These training zones are only a guide, so don't worry about being overly precise with heart rates because they'll fluctuate anyway. It's good to be mindful of your intensity but it's even more important that you get out there and enjoy your training.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":613.8776169187748,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":310.62989999999996,"r":539.3339,"t":642.4624536078127},"charspan":[0,250],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/43","text":"These training zones are only a guide, so don't worry about being overly precise with heart rates because they'll fluctuate anyway. It's good to be mindful of your intensity but it's even more important that you get out there and enjoy your training."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"ZONE 1 [Z1] Recovery","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":600.7106169187748,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":310.62989999999996,"r":376.46490000000006,"t":606.8044536078128},"charspan":[0,20],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/44","text":"ZONE 1 [Z1] Recovery"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"60 to 65% of your maximum. Easy pace, feels nice and light.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":593.2136169187748,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":310.62989999999996,"r":486.7148999999985,"t":599.3074536078128},"charspan":[0,59],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/45","text":"60 to 65% of your maximum. Easy pace, feels nice and light."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"ZONE 2 [Z2] Steady","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":580.0466169187748,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":310.62989999999996,"r":370.9278999999999,"t":586.1404536078128},"charspan":[0,18],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/46","text":"ZONE 2 [Z2] Steady"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"65 to 75% of your maximum. Fairly easy pace. Easy enough so that you could breathe just through your nose if you wanted to.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":565.0526169187749,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":310.6299,"r":538.5849,"t":578.6434536078128},"charspan":[0,123],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/47","text":"65 to 75% of your maximum. Fairly easy pace. Easy enough so that you could breathe just through your nose if you wanted to."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"ZONE 3 [Z3] Tempo","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":551.8856169187749,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":310.6299,"r":371.6489000000001,"t":557.9794536078128},"charspan":[0,17],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/48","text":"ZONE 3 [Z3] Tempo"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"75% to 80% of your maximum. A fairly hard but sustainable pace.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":544.3886169187749,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":310.6229,"r":503.6058999999985,"t":550.4824536078129},"charspan":[0,63],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/49","text":"75% to 80% of your maximum. A fairly hard but sustainable pace."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"ZONE 4 [Z4] Race tempo","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":531.2216169187749,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":310.6229,"r":386.98589999999973,"t":537.3154536078129},"charspan":[0,22],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/50","text":"ZONE 4 [Z4] Race tempo"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"80 to 90% of your maximum. A hard pace that requires real focus to sustain.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":515.723616918775,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":310.6229,"r":504.4598999999998,"t":529.8184536078129},"charspan":[0,75],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/51","text":"80 to 90% of your maximum. A hard pace that requires real focus to sustain."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"KEY WU Warm up, WD Warm down, MAIN Main set, FC Front  crawl, KICK Kick with a float held out in front of you, BUILD Gradually increase the intensity of each rep within a set, PULL Front crawl with a pull float between thighs, RI Rest interval, BACK Backstroke, BREAST Breaststroke, 1-ARM Front crawl using one arm only N/S Negative split  -  swim  the  2nd  half  faster  than  the  first, FDRAG Drag  your fingers along the surface during the FC arm recovery, FISTS Swim FC with clenched fists, DOG Doggy paddle, SCULL Kick  with  arms  held  out  in  front,  sculling  your hands side to side, BAND Front  crawl  with  a  rubber  band  or  inner-tube  tied  around ankles, ANKLES Front crawl with pull float between ankles","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":439.08061691877487,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":310.60890000000006,"r":546.3479000000001,"t":505.15045360781284},"charspan":[0,725],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/52","text":"KEY WU Warm up, WD Warm down, MAIN Main set, FC Front  crawl, KICK Kick with a float held out in front of